# OHGO Documentation Migration

> **Status:** complete.
> **Scope:** repository documentation only. No implementation package, source
> behaviour, API, persistence format, provider, TUI, CLI, or test was changed.
> **Result:** the active documentation surface is 19 Markdown files; 51 tracked
> historical documents and 3 git-ignored local port logs moved to
> `old_docs/`, which is a temporary archive for human removal.

---

## 1. Summary

The repository had accumulated three documentation layers that no longer shared
one authority model:

1. current product and contributor documentation (`README.md`, `AGENTS.md`,
   `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `docs/RELEASING.md`);
2. current architecture governance (`OHGO_ARCHITECTURE_MAP.md`,
   `OHGO_ARCHITECTURE_RULES.md`, `OHGO_ARCHITECTURE_MIGRATION.md`);
3. a large body of port-era plans, phase reports, benchmark artifacts, and
   pre-migration architecture snapshots.

All three layers were active and discoverable. Several current documents still
linked to the pre-`internal/` architecture or duplicated facts that now have a
canonical owner. The cleanup established one canonical source per subject,
kept the current behavioural references, and moved completed/historical
material behind the explicit `old_docs/` boundary.

### Scale

| Item | Before | After |
|---|---:|---:|
| Active Markdown files (excluding `old_docs/`) | 69 tracked + 3 local | 19 |
| Archived Markdown files | 0 | 55 (including the archive marker) |
| Archived non-Markdown files | 0 | 41 benchmark result/script files |
| Canonical architecture documents | 3 | 3 (unchanged set, clarified roles) |
| Deleted documents | — | 0; one ignored OS metadata file removed |

In addition to the 69 tracked Markdown files, three root documents were
untracked and git-ignored (`MEMORY.md`, `PORT.md`, `PROGRESS.md`) only in the
working tree. They were still part of the local documentation surface and were
archived.

