## 4. What was consolidated

| Consolidation | Why |
|---|---|
| `README.md` architecture section now links to the three canonical architecture documents instead of presenting `docs/architecture/ARCHITECTURE.md` as the system map. | The README is an entry point, not a competing architecture authority. |
| `docs/architecture/ARCHITECTURE.md` was reframed from “the map” to “runtime behaviour reference” and its package-layer diagram was removed. | The diagram duplicated `OHGO_ARCHITECTURE_MAP.md`; the file now keeps only behaviour that has no other owner. |
| All five `docs/architecture/*.md` documents now declare the same canonical topology/rules links and defer package ownership to the map. | One topology authority; supporting documents explain subjects rather than redefine the tree. |
| `CONTRIBUTING.md` now points to `AGENTS.md` and the canonical architecture documents, and its provider/tool paths were corrected to `internal/...`. | Removes duplicate, stale operational instructions without deleting the contributor checklist. |
| `docs/RELEASING.md` now lists the map, rules, and migration record in the documentation-update matrix. | Release changes update the canonical source, not an obsolete “system contract”. |
| `AGENTS.md` gained a short documentation-discipline section. | Future contributors know where facts belong and that `old_docs/` is not active. |

No new architecture document was invented. The existing canonical set already
had the right semantic split.

