## 9. Documentation gaps

These gaps remain and are recorded rather than filled with guessed content:

1. **No automated documentation-governance test.** The repository already
   machine-checks code architecture through `internal/architecture`. It has no
   equivalent check for canonical-file existence, links into `old_docs/`, or
   removed paths. Adding one is recommended, but it would be a test/code change
   outside this task’s documentation-only boundary.
2. **Source comments still cite `ARCHITECTURE_CONTRACT_V1` section numbers.**
   `internal/memory/memory.go`, `internal/tui/permissions.go`,
   `internal/prompt/prompt.go`, and `internal/control/workspace/workspace.go`
   contain rationale comments referencing the archived contract. They still
   describe real decisions, but a future comment-only cleanup should retarget
   them at `OHGO_ARCHITECTURE_RULES.md`.
3. **The repository benchmark harness is historically stale.** 
   `bench/repository/tasks.go` contains pre-migration target paths
   (`ai/openai.go`, `task/view.go`) and a documentation target at
   `docs/architecture/ARCHITECTURE.md` line 23 whose expected phrase moved when
   the duplicate layer map was removed; `bench/repository/main.go` still emits
   results under `docs/benchmarks/results`. The harness is not part of the
   active documentation set and was not modified.
4. **No separate CLI/TUI reference manual.** The README documents the current
   flags, slash commands, terminal modes, and completion verdicts; there is no
   exhaustive per-command API reference. This was already true before the
   cleanup and is not fabricated here.
5. **The runtime reference is deliberately broad.** 
   `docs/architecture/ARCHITECTURE.md` was canonicalized for ownership and
   paths, but the implementation and tests remain the final authority for
   behavioural detail. It is a supporting reference, not a second contract.

